\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 1. The transfer of EPR Certificates has been resumed and is operational on the EPR Portal. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 2. Single Sign-On (SSO) for EPR Portals is live now. Please login through the SSO at \"),e.I0R(59,\"a\",39),e.OEk(60,\"https://epr.cpcb.gov.in\"),e.C$Y(),e.OEk(61,\" to access all EPR Portals. FAQs and User Manuals are now uploaded on the Common EPR Portal. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 3. The provision for deletion of procurement, production, and sales entries in PWP Operations has now been enabled on the EPR Portal. All PWPs are advised to utilize this feature to remove incorrect entries pertaining to the ongoing Financial Years. Please note that the deletion option will remain available only until the sales invoice has been uploaded. All existing validations across PWP operation modules shall remain unchanged. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 4. In case any user has sent an email to EPR helpdesk regarding issues faced on the EPR plastic portal and the same has not been resolved, till date, users are required to lodge a complaint through the ticket module developed by CPCB, for resolution of the same. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 \"),e.OEk(62,\" 5. This is to inform that if your User Account has been locked due to multiple in-correct entries of Password/ OTP, then it will automatically get unlocked after 24 hrs. Tickets may not be raised for the same. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 6. Provision for Change of Login credentials (When original Phone No. and /or email are not accessible) has been made on the EPR Plastic Portal. Please refer to the document \\u201cInstruction sheet for Change of Login credentials (When original Phone No. and /or email are not accessible) \\u201c uploaded on the \\u201c EPR Plastic Portal\\u201d for further details on the matter. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 7. The Producer/Importer can now upload sales transaction data by scanning the QR code on the GST e-Invoice using the mobile app 'Centralised EPR Plastic(CEPP)' app. The app is available on Google Playstore. Please refer to the instruction sheet uploaded in Important Documents section on the EPR portal. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 8. \\u2060In continuation of Show Cause Notice issued(SCN) on December 30, 2024, this is to inform that the timeline for filing Annual Returns (AR) by PIBOs & PWPs for FY 2023-24 has been extended to January 31, 2025. All concerned PIBOs/PWPs are requested to file their AR within the stipulated time to avoid levying of EC Charges as per details given in the SCN dated December 30, 2024. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 9. PWPs are required to ensure that valid GST eInvoice of the finished products, which are clearly visible and readable, is uploaded in the sales section of the EPR portal. Please refer to the 'Instruction Sheet (PWP Sales)' uploaded in the \\u2018Important Documents\\u2019 section on the portal. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 10. Producers in the micro & small category do not have to fulfil EPR Obligations w.e.f. FY 2023-24 onwards. They are however required to file AR for FY 2023-24. \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 11. As per updated EC Guidelines, if the PIBOs/ PWPs are not able to file AR due to Force Majeure conditions, final decision regarding levying of EC on such PIBOs/ PWPs shall be taken by the Committee constituted for the purpose \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 12. Meeting with Stakeholders for addressing EPR related issues to be conducted everyday from 4.00 P.M to 5.00 P.M from Monday to Saturday. \"),e.I0R(63,\"a\",40),e.OEk(64,\"Click here to join\"),e.C$Y(),e.OEk(65,\" \\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0\\xa0 \"),e.C$Y()()(),e.yuY(66,vl,9,2,\"section\",41),e.I0R(67,\"section\",42)(68,\"div\",43)(69,\"div\",44)(70,\"div\",45)(71,\"div\",46)(72,\"h5\",47),e.OEk(73,\" About CPCB \"),e.C$Y(),e.I0R(74,\"p\",48),e.OEk(75,\" The Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB), statutory organisation, was constituted in September, 1974 under the Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1974. Further, CPCB was entrusted with the powers and functions under the Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981. \"),e.wR5(76,\"br\"),e.C$Y(),e.I0R(77,\"div\",49)(78,\"a\",50)(79,\"button\",51),e.OEk(80,\" Learn More \"),e.C$Y()()()()(),e.I0R(81,\"div\",45)(82,\"div\",52)(83,\"div\",53)(84,\"h5\",54),e.OEk(85,\" Contact Us \"),e.C$Y(),e.wR5(86,\"div\",55),e.I0R(87,\"form\",56),e.qCj(\"submit\",function(){return n.onSubmit()}),e.I0R(88,\"div\",53)(89,\"div\",57)(90,\"div\",58)(91,\"label\",59),e.OEk(92,\"Name\"),e.C$Y()(),e.I0R(93,\"div\",60)(94,\"div\",61),e.wR5(95,\"input\",62),e.C$Y(),e.yuY(96,bl,2,1,\"div\",63),e.C$Y()()(),e.I0R(97,\"div\",64)(98,\"div\",65)(99,\"div\",66)(100,\"div\")(101,\"label\",59),e.OEk(102,\"Email\"),e.C$Y()(),e.I0R(103,\"div\",60)(104,\"div\",61),e.wR5(105,\"input\",67),e.C$Y(),e.yuY(106,Rl,3,2,\"div\",63),e.C$Y()(),e.I0R(107,\"div\",68)(108,\"div\")(109,\"label\",59),e.OEk(110,\"Mobile\"),e.C$Y()(),e.I0R(111,\"div\",69)(112,\"div\",61)(113,\"input\",70),e.qCj(\"keypress\",function(l){return n.numberAllow(l)}),e.C$Y()(),e.yuY(114,Pl,3,2,\"div\",63),e.C$Y()()()(),e.I0R(115,\"div\",0)(116,\"div\",71)(117,\"div\",72)(118,\"label\",59),e.OEk(119,\"Subject\"),e.C$Y()(),e.I0R(120,\"div\",73)(121,\"div\",74)(122,\"textarea\",75),e.OEk(123,\"                          \"),e.C$Y()(),e.yuY(124,Tl,2,1,\"div\",63),e.C$Y()()(),e.I0R(125,